      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I cant disagree that the platform needs money and im sure some people want to encourage it, but I still fear things like parts of worlds being locked behind such checks or even potentially entire worlds. Maybe even in reverse if someone is spiteful, restricting someone from parts of a world or the entire world if they were a subscriber.\n\nIm not opposed to it if people are just going to do cosmetic things, but I've seen worlds already paywall things like media players, or even literal closet rooms. I don't want to further see things be gated behind stuff like vrc+ (again a world creator won't even benefit profit wise from this).\n\nIt makes me wonder what exactly youre trying to implement though?",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
